   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "ROBERTS-HORNE MEDICAL GROUP - DISCHARGE SUMMARY\n\nPatient: John Mccullough \nDOB: 07/11/1969 \nSex: M \nMRN: 141460\n\nAdmit Date: 01/15/2002 \nDischarge Date: 04/02/2026\n\nProvider: Dr. Maria Sanchez, family medicine, Roberts-Horne Medical Group\n\n---\n\n**Principal Diagnosis:** \nNon-kidney organ transplant (24.3 years ago; organ other)\n\n**Secondary Diagnoses:** \nNone\n\n---\n\n**Admission Details:** \nMr. John Mccullough, a 56-year-old male with a history of a non-kidney organ transplant performed 24.3 years ago, was admitted on 01/15/2002 for routine follow-up and management of his transplant. \n\n**Hospital Course:** \nMr. Mccullough's hospital course was largely uneventful. He presented for his scheduled follow-up visit related to his transplant on 04/02/2026. His vital signs upon admission were stable with a blood pressure of 112/77 mmHg and a weight of 169 pounds. \n\nDuring his visit, Mr. Mccullough reported no acute complaints. His physical examination was unremarkable except for expected post-transplant findings. He denied any chest pain, shortness of breath, or significant changes in his overall health status. \n\nHowever, it is noted that Mr. Mccullough has been non-compliant with his medications, specifically cyclosporine and sirolimus, and has missed two follow-up appointments. This non-compliance has been a recurrent issue and was addressed during his visit. \n\n**Medications at Discharge:** \n- Cyclosporine 100 mg daily\n- Sirolimus 1 mg daily\n\n**Procedures:** \nNo procedures were performed during this admission. \n\n**Discharge Plan:** \nMr. Mccullough was discharged home in stable condition. He was counseled on the importance of medication adherence and the risks associated with non-compliance. A follow-up appointment was scheduled for 06/02/2026 to monitor his transplant status and ensure he is adhering to his medication regimen. \n\n**Social History:** \n- Tobacco use: Former cigarette smoker, 1 pack per day, quit on 02/15/2017.\n- Alcohol use: Approximately 1 drink per week.\n\n**Follow-Up:** \nMr. Mccullough is to follow up with Dr. Maria Sanchez at the Roberts-Horne Medical Group on 06/02/2026. He was instructed to contact the office immediately if he experiences any concerning symptoms such as fever, unexpected weight gain, or signs of infection.\n\n**Additional Notes:** \n- Mr. Mccullough’s weight has fluctuated slightly over the past year, ranging from 167 to 177 pounds. \n- His blood pressure has remained within normal limits during recent visits, with the highest recorded being 118/83 mmHg and the lowest 102/76 mmHg.\n- He has had several minor compla"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "ints in the past, including a back strain in October 2025 and a URI in May 2025, both of which resolved with conservative management.\n\n---\n\nThis discharge summary reflects Mr. Mccullough's current health status and the need for continued monitoring and adherence to his medication regimen to ensure the longevity and functionality of his transplanted organ.\n"
    }
